Fixed. The package doc now states the disable case explicitly rather than implying the refresher always runs:

```go
// endpoints, and BifrostHTTPServer.startLiveModelRefresher, which re-fetches
// every provider on the configured live_models_sync_interval unless that
// interval is 0, which disables the refresher.
```

Went with naming the sentinel rather than a bare "when enabled" so the doc matches the two other places that describe this field: `modelcatalog/config.go` ("LiveModelsSyncDisabled (0) turns the background refresher off entirely") and `transports/config.schema.json` ("Set to 0 to disable background refresh").

